node_modules/
data/
client/dist/
.env
.DS_Store
*.log

# Excel lock files, created whenever someone has a workbook open.
~$*

# Real rosters and past master schedules — these carry participant names and
# contact details and must never reach this repo, which is public.
# Anonymized fixtures derived from them live in fixtures/ and ARE committed.
samples/

# Working spreadsheets at the repo root. These are the drafts logistics fills
# in, so they start as placeholders and end up holding ~280 real names and
# phone numbers. Ignoring the whole root pattern rather than the two current
# filenames on purpose: the next draft someone saves alongside them is covered
# without anyone having to remember this file exists.
#
# Root level only — fixtures/*.xlsx stays committable, which is where a
# spreadsheet safe to publish belongs.
/*.xlsx

# The blank template IS committed. It is the deliverable logistics fills in, and
# tests/template.test.js reads it to check that its tabs and columns still match
# what the importer looks for — so if it stops being tracked, that check stops
# being run anywhere but this laptop.
#
# ⚠️ It is committed on the understanding that the *filled* copy lives in Google
# Sheets and never comes back here. Anything else that lands in templates/ is
# assumed to be a filled-in copy carrying ~280 real names and phone numbers, and
# is ignored on that basis. If you have to work on a filled copy locally, keep
# it out of this directory.
/templates/*
!/templates/royalty-schedule-template.xlsx
